	affiliations = {School of Biomedical Engineering, BK21 Plus Research Institute of Biomedical Engineering, Konkuk University, Chungju, 380-701, South Korea; Department of Organic Materials and Fiber Engineering, College of Engineering, Soongsil University, Seoul, 356-743, South Korea; Department of Biomedical Engineering, Jungwon University, Goesan, 367-805, South Korea},
	abstract = {Gait disturbance is typical symptom of the degenerative cerebropathia such as Alzheimer's disease, dementia, and Parkinson's disease. Thus measuring the activity of the knee joint is important to make a diagnosis for these diseases. In this study, the fiber-optic goniometer was developed using a plastic optical fiber, a light emitting diode, and a photodiode to measure knee joint angles. To evaluate the fiber-optic goniometer, we measured knee angles using the fiber-optic goniometer and 3-D IR motion camera in walking and cycling. As a result, patterns of knee joint angle obtained by the fiber-optic goniometer during walking and cycling corresponded with those obtained by the 3-D IR motion camera. In terms of sampling resolution and error occurrence, the fiber-optic goniometer fabricated through this study can be used in diagnosis of degenerative cerebropathia. Copyright © 2015 American Scientific Publishers All rights reserved.},
