	abstract = {Rapid cycling is a relatively unusual presentation of bipolar affective disorder in the elderly. After a historical revision and an analysis of recent nosologies (ICD-10, DSM-IV), four cases of rapid cycling affective disorder in elderly women (aged from 78 to 86) are presented. Two of them began illness in the adulthood (30 and 49 years old), and rapid cycles appeared secondary in the elderly (76 and 82). The two others began their illness immediately in rapid cycles respectively at the age of 62 and 66. Only one had evidence of dementia process associated to the mood disorder. Early onset secondary rapid cyclicity seems to have more successfully responded to prophylactic treatment, respectively by carbamazepine and valproate.},
